hipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MD"},{"bioguideId":"F000479","fullName":"Sen. Fetterman, John [D-PA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"PA"},{"bioguideId":"M000133","fullName":"Sen. Markey, Edward J. [D-MA]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MA"},{"bioguideId":"W000779","fullName":"Sen. Wyden, Ron [D-OR]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"},{"bioguideId":"H001042","fullName":"Sen. Hirono, Mazie K. [D-HI]","isOriginalCosponsor":true,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"HI"},{"bioguideId":"D000563","fullName":"Sen. Durbin, Richard J. [D-IL]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-01","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"S001194","fullName":"Sen. Schatz, Brian [D-HI]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-07-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"HI"},{"bioguideId":"B001288","fullName":"Sen. Booker, Cory A. [D-NJ]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"A000382","fullName":"Sen. Alsobrooks, Angela D. [D-MD]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MD"},{"bioguideId":"K000394","fullName":"Sen. Kim, Andy [D-NJ]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NJ"},{"bioguideId":"M001176","fullName":"Sen. Merkley, Jeff [D-OR]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-16","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OR"},{"bioguideId":"C001088","fullName":"Sen. Coons, Christopher A. [D-DE]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"DE"},{"bioguideId":"S001208","fullName":"Sen. Slotkin, Elissa [D-MI]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-09-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MI"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T06:17:44+00:00","id":"s1370-119","introducedDate":"2025-04-09","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-04-09","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Finance."},"laws":[],"number":"1370","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Crime and Law Enforcement","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"H001046","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Heinrich, Martin [D-NM]","party":"D","state":"NM"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-04-09","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Gas-Operated Semi-Automatic Firearms Exclusion Act or the GOSAFE Act</strong></p><p>This bill establishes a framework to regulate gas-operated semiautomatic firearms and large capacity ammunition feeding devices under federal firearms laws.</p><p>First, the bill generally prohibits the import, sale, manufacture, transfer, receipt, or possession of</p><ul><li>a firearm that is or is modified to operate as a prohibited gas-operated semiautomatic firearm;</li><li>a combination of parts that modify or can be&nbsp;assembled into&nbsp;a prohibited gas-operated semiautomatic firearm, or that produce an unlawful gas-operated semiautomatic cycling action;</li><li>a device or combination of parts designed to materially increase the rate of fire of a semiautomatic firearm; or</li><li>a firearm that is modified to materially increase the rate of fire.</li></ul><p>Second, the bill generally prohibits (1) the import, sale, manufacture, transfer, or receipt of a large capacity ammunition feeding device; or (2) the possession of a large capacity ammunition feeding device manufactured after the date of enactment.&nbsp;</p><p>A violation is subject to criminal penalties—a fine, a prison term of up to 12 months, or both, for each violation.&nbsp;</p><p>In addition, an individual who possesses a prohibited gas-operated semiautomatic firearm during a&nbsp;federal felony offense is subject to additional penalties—a&nbsp;fine, a mandatory minimum prison term of two years, or both.</p><p>Finally, the bill allows a state or local government to use Edward Byrne Memorial Justice Assistance Grant Program funds to compensate individuals who surrender gas-operated semiautomatic firearms and large capacity ammunition feeding devices under a buy-back program.</p>","updateDate":"2026-05-15T18:24:26Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"GOSAFE Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2026-09-16T11:03:39Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-16T11:03:39Z"}
